  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_3dfda7b0f3b3425fa5dc8750c18d2ef0",
      "statement": "Each cell has one ownership record at cells/<cell>/own.json that names the owner node's session and carries a fencing epoch; a None node is a deliberately released, fenced record, and epochs never reset.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L289-L289",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:58f41f00c48a266f178b4fc010579bfdd352f003de0cf9d6de27ea5ac399977f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L138-L144",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56908733e39222aa35a8d351008f198cd775b060de0626da25cd87d16df6b598:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d8846310f0d401eb08bd32cbd93c7a7",
      "statement": "A node acquires a cell with a conditional write (create when absent, compare-and-swap on the previous record), and every activation advances the epoch, so an epoch never has two writers and two nodes cannot acquire the same cell.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L108-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:867aa55245397481450b264390ce610cbe84b9e7919c828124b722c7f1c2df98:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L116-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:02a173bb2ec88ff41e741837bf053893627c5f64ee1828ff288c48b3cc5179d8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4494e2f21f274628915453f0a318985b",
      "statement": "An ambiguous ownership compare-and-swap is re-read rather than retried blindly, and each claim may reconcile an ambiguous acquire at most MAX_ACQUIRE_RECONCILES (3) times before the request fails with AcquireFailed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L24-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab02bb05e0fdce99e7eff833c1403f60eeaf3df2ef71e083461530aa27f303d3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L3674-L3696",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0b4e13e9158a3b37a85a9945e1ac3c5f8b6eb73c9bff08e6dd1b5fd80cff8f4d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88ad2711c33540a8b182462b4e282177",
      "statement": "The protocol requires a conditional create, a conditional overwrite, and read-after-write consistency from the object store; stores without working conditional writes cannot fence a cell, so two nodes can then both own one cell.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L16-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba4417465d008614904352ba5acf5ceae298452b5f5617937290605df8a4994e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_299b519d36e8410c98ae90ee844b0e82",
      "statement": "Replicated data lives under cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/ with the epoch in the key as the fence, so a node that lost ownership can keep writing but only into a superseded prefix that a restore does not select.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L120-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c7ea0b8a9de921d82d3d2ebf02c1bbf4e2b15d8545052517581f200eb5bb3e6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_748214d3c0244fddb302059014f25405",
      "statement": "Each node holds a lease at nodes/<node>.json carrying an expiry, advertised address, peer protocol version, and per-process generation, renewed after one third of the lifetime (CELLD_TTL_MS, default 10000 ms).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L146-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d85c4c874e50d4afddc1261945885ce00db6a8d9fa32200853691cfc7cd51d8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L200-L204",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fdaa0ed976fb778ec678b6b73a347e65ad856ab1f1fa92ef9837ed54580cef09:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fd85a2d7a92e403f8e29c7888fc31545",
      "statement": "Node authority is the lease's published validity evaluated at ask time on the monotonic clock, so a request is refused the instant the lease lapses even before the fence timer fires.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L723-L742",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c1f052bc041d9b1e293be85302fdc7304b7441310721edf1e732eead9ac81b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5bb175dbd2b646a29fc78e8e1acadaa0",
      "statement": "A lease renewal that lands at or after the prior lease's expiry fences the node rather than resurrecting the lease, because a peer may already have begun a takeover — the gap is treated as a fence, not a hiccup.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L1857-L1891",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78c9f2ff515759cb32761d917d2a489f409199eb67123fea7c5a7db7fb264d33:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b8e1b8aa89cc4d00969374fa1aa8dfe9",
      "statement": "A node that cannot renew its lease fences itself when its published expiry passes (or at once if another writer replaced its record), stopping each active cell and failing every uncompleted request; a fenced node logs SELF-FENCE: and exits with code 3.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L5076-L5149",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e72e1d30bdd94143787ce90491f3f5f913dce7ee50295fbbade09d43cb0ecd4f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L236-L244",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e9c2f581752e05c09bbc72b975fb48a5a43b86b309cf05123c741b278d89aea:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L208-L212",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c95664b1fb96b38d6e06da0a92eb0ee55694843c827e7d2c4e23f6949a64188:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_81b211e9e5c54564be106091ab463e35",
      "statement": "The fence writes nothing to the bucket; peers already read the lease as dead or replaced and acquire the cells through the ownership records, and a request is safe before the fence runs because routing compares the current time against the published expiry each time it routes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L214-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:becf2fecd4ae3737c64b59dc7df6f8bb3b5774a60cb55c0c3d14bf6bc3279e68:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ff1a2101c779404faf92e7bf954bd3e9",
      "statement": "A takeover first collects whatever the stopped node had not uploaded through the node-log recovery gate before restoring; an eviction or shutdown handoff can also publish a cell unowned (Effect::ReleaseOwner, keeping its epoch) and ask a compatible peer to acquire it (Effect::AdoptReleased).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L806-L819",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eddbe146be1624ed85301bd9bd428ca025f49c17766ae49442e9cb13e023f816:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L61-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93a7759aa23d1fac35be44e243db7f9c05d6881882916fd3d81c5b84e4793601:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5036ba55530146a09b8e038e7e1f926f",
      "statement": "There is no join service or fixed membership list; nodes find each other through the node leases in the bucket, and ownership resolution reads the owner record and a peer's lease for its address and protocol version.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L320-L350",
